---
// Chains.astro - JSON-RPC read as JSON-RPC: the part a general proxy leaves as
// hex. Everything here is in the window today.
---

<section class="section" id="chains">
  <div class="container chains-inner">
    <div class="chains-text">
      <span class="eyebrow">JSON-RPC</span>
      <h2>Four bytes of hex, read as the call they are</h2>
      <p class="bento-text">
        A node answers in words nobody reads: a <code>data</code> field of hex, a
        signed transaction as RLP, a revert that came back with status 200. tracewing
        reads them where they stand, and lets you write them back the same way.
      </p>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>
          Calldata named and laid out — <code>balanceOf(0xd8dA…)</code> with its
          arguments — by the calls every chain shares, or by an ABI you choose in
          Settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          A signed transaction out of its RLP, with <strong>who signed it</strong>{' '}
          recovered from the signature, amounts in ether, fees in gwei and addresses
          in their EIP-55 capitals.
        </li>
        <li>
          Solana and Bitcoin too: base58 and lamports, a transaction's own id worked
          out from its bytes, and the accounts a program was given.
        </li>
        <li>
          Write a call out in Compose — or in a message to an open socket — and it
          goes as the calldata it stands for.
        </li>
        <li>
          A warning when an edit has left a signature over bytes that are gone, with
          the address the signature now works out to instead. tracewing holds no
          keys and signs nothing.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <figure class="chains-shot">
      <img
        src="/shots/rpc.webp"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        alt="The inspector reading a JSON-RPC call: the function it names, its arguments, and the transaction's fields."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .chains-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .chains-text h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .chains-text > .bento-text {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .chains-shot {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .chains-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
  }

  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .chains-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
